.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# =========================
# Go
# =========================
# `go build ./services/<name>/...` run from the repo root drops an
# unadorned binary named after the package at the CURRENT directory (the
# repo root), not inside services/<name>/ — easy to do by accident and
# easy to not notice before staging. Named explicitly, not a wildcard,
# so a legitimately-named source directory is never at risk of being
# ignored by mistake.
/provider-stub
/provider-gateway
/provider-fake
# Same accident, but from `go build ./...` run FROM WITHIN a service's own
# directory instead of the repo root — hit this for real during Phase-03
# Step A6.
/services/provider-fake/provider-fake
/services/provider-gateway/provider-gateway

